<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emancipation reform of 1861</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1861">1861</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Emancipation Edict</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The emancipation reform of 1861 was the decree of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-ii-of-russia">Alexander II</a> abolishing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serfdom">serfdom</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>. It freed millions of peasants, though they had to pay redemption for land, and it opened a period of wider reforms in local government, the courts and the army.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emancipation-reform-of-1861.jpg" alt="Emancipation reform of 1861" width="320" height="236" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Boris Kustodiev · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reading_of_the_Manifest_(Liberation_of_peasants)_-_Kustodiev,_1907.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
